TRIGGER CONDITIONS

A commercial license from the Licensor is required if your use of the Licensed
Work meets ANY of the following conditions:

1. DEVICE COUNT
   You deploy or operate the Licensed Work to coordinate more than ten (10)
   compute devices or ten (10) inference nodes within a single production system or
   across systems controlled by the same legal entity.

2. MANAGED SERVICE / HOSTED OFFERING
   You offer access to the Licensed Work, or to a product or service that
   substantially incorporates the Licensed Work, to third parties over a
   network (e.g. as software-as-a-service, platform-as-a-service, or a managed
   inference API), regardless of the number of devices involved.

3. OEM / SOFTWARE DISTRIBUTION
   You embed, bundle, or distribute the Licensed Work, in whole or in part, as
   a component of a commercial software product or service that you provide to
   third-party customers, whether as a standalone product, a subscription
   service, or otherwise.

4. COMPETING PRODUCT
   You use the Licensed Work, or any substantial portion of it, as the basis
   for a commercial AI inference orchestration or fleet management product or
   service that competes with the Licensor's offerings.

For commercial licensing enquiries, contact: pberlizov@college.harvard.edu

